<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to November 4, partly to balance a rise in bank note circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the  weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   413.73 (+  1.35)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  12.28 (+  0.85)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  3.18 (-  0.05)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.32 (unchanged)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 107.39 (+  4.02)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   448.06 (+  2.50)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
